  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "While the design methodology is intended for tropical Asia, the physical and biological testing was limited to Sri Lankan roofing standards and specific local grass species.",
      "what": "Researchers engineered and tested a lightweight, modular vegetative roof tile measuring 900 mm × 1200 mm with a wave-shaped corrugated profile to replace conventional sloped roofing materials in Sri Lanka. The fiber-reinforced plastic tile has a depth of 2.5 cm and a total saturated weight of 52.5 kg/m², meeting Eurocode structural standards. Biological testing demonstrated a 100% survival rate and over 80% canopy coverage for the grass species Axonopus compressus and Zoysia matrella.",
      "why": "This design provides a direct structural replacement for conventional sloped roofs, bypassing the high structural conversion costs and slope limitations that previously prevented the adoption of green roofs in tropical Asian cities."
